# Spark DS — Foundations

Use foundation docs before picking type, space, or elevation values.

| Topic | Doc | Token prefix |
|-------|-----|--------------|
| Colors | `colors.html` | `--semantic-content-*`, `--semantic-surface-*` |
| Typography | `typography.html` | `--semantic-typography-*` |
| Dimensions | `dimensions.html` | `--primitive-space-*`, component layout tokens |
| Shadows | `shadows-effects.html` | `--semantic-shadow-*` |

## Typography

- Font family: Figtree via `--semantic-typography-*-font-family`.
- Headings: `--semantic-typography-heading-1-font-size` through `heading-5`.
- Body: `--semantic-typography-body-*`. Detail/caption: `--semantic-typography-detail-*`.
- Do not set arbitrary `font-size`, `font-weight`, or `line-height` when a semantic token exists.

## Layout and spacing

- Use the spacing scale in `dimensions.html` (`--primitive-space-1` through `--primitive-space-10`). Avoid magic numbers (`margin: 13px`).
- For components, prefer scoped layout tokens (e.g. `--semantic-button-padding-x-medium`, `--semantic-button-gap-icon-label-medium`).
- Canvas background: `--semantic-surface-canvas`. Cards/panels: `--semantic-surface-white` or `--semantic-surface-muted`.

## Shadows and focus

- Elevation: `--semantic-shadow-*` from `shadows-effects.html`.
- Focus rings: `--semantic-shadow-focus-ring-neutral` or component-specific focus tokens.

## React example

```css
.pageTitle {
  font-family: var(--semantic-typography-heading-font-family);
  font-size: var(--semantic-typography-heading-2-font-size);
  line-height: var(--semantic-typography-heading-2-line-height);
  font-weight: var(--semantic-typography-heading-font-weight);
  color: var(--semantic-content-primary);
}
```
